# Your own token rules. Upgrades replace key_prefixes.rules and keep this
# file. pf apply installs the two as one, with this file second. The
# broker, the engine, pf dns and pf observe read the result.
#
#   name	regexp	[KIND]
#
# Use the format of key_prefixes.rules. Start each rule with a literal
# prefix, for example acme_. pf apply refuses a rule that does not
# compile or that has no literal prefix. Write a length as a minimum
# ({32,}), with no closing \b. Give the KIND of the token when a core
# host injects it, so that the fence does not strip it on that host.
#
#   acme	acme_[A-Za-z0-9]{32,}	ACME_TOKEN
